<title>USA: Cellular Communications stake sold.</title>
<headline>Cellular Communications stake sold.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by Southport, Conn., investment adviser Dawson-Samberg Capital Management Inc. said Tuesday that it sold its entire stake in Cellular Communications International Inc.</p>
<p>In a filing with the the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said it sold 549,350 shares, or about 5.41 percent of the total, on Nov. 21 at $26.25 a share.</p>
<p>On Feb. 17, 1995, the group reported that it held 639,750 shares, or 6.30 percent.</p>
</text>
